The JSON configuration snippet for encryption at rest is the same in all five passages (Sections 1, 6, 11, 16, and 21 of the Security Policy Handbook) [1][2][3][4][5]. It contains a single top-level object, `encryption_at_rest`, with two settings:

- `"enabled": true`, which turns encryption at rest on.
- `"timeout_ms": 5000`, which sets the request timeout to 5000 milliseconds.

```json
{
  "encryption_at_rest": {
    "enabled": true,
    "timeout_ms": 5000
  }
}
```

The snippet leaves out `max_retries`. The accompanying tables list it with a default of 3, but it does not appear in the JSON [1][2][3][4][5].
